claim.claim-text:
a movable end effector (302);
a processing head (310) mounted to the movable end effector (320);
a position sensor (332) configured to determine real-time positions of the processing head (310) and output sensor signals indicative thereof; and
a system controller (304) operatively connected to the movable end effector (302), the position sensor (332), and the processing head (310), the system controller (304) being programmed to:

determine a plurality of joint locations for the superposed wires (140, 142);
command the movable end effector (302) to sequentially move the processing head (310) to align the processing head (310) with each of the joint locations;
receive, from the position sensor (332), the sensor signals indicative of the real-time positions of the processing head (310);
determine, from the received sensor signals and a captured image of the workpiece (132'), an estimated distance between each of the real-time positions of the processing head (310) and a next adjacent one of the joint locations;
estimate a plurality of desired trajectories for the processing head (310) each based on the estimated distance between the real-time position of the processing head (310) and the respective next adjacent one of the joint locations; and
command the processing head (310) to join the superposed wires (140, 142) at the joint locations to form the engineered textile (132).

receiving a workpiece (132') composed of superposed wires (140, 142);
determining, via a system controller (304), a plurality of joint locations for the superposed wires (140, 142);
commanding, via the system controller (304), a movable end effector (302) to sequentially move a processing head (310) to thereby align the processing head (310) with each of the joint locations;
receiving, via the system controller (304) from a position sensor (332), sensor signals indicative of real-time positions of the processing head (310);
determining, via the system controller (304) from the received sensor signals and a captured image of the workpiece (132'), an estimated distance between each of the real-time positions of the processing head (310) and a next adjacent one of the joint locations;
estimating, via the system controller (304), a plurality of desired trajectories for the processing head (310) each based on the estimated distance between the real-time position of the processing head (310) and the respective next adjacent one of the joint locations; and
commanding, via the system controller (304), the processing head (310) to join the superposed wires (140, 142) at the joint locations to form the engineered textile (132).
